      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**The problem:** The usual adult dose of amlodipine is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and **10 mg/day is the maximum**. 50 mg is 5 times the maximum. Doses that high can cause severe low blood pressure, shock and heart rhythm problems. Amlodipine overdoses are especially hard to treat because the drug stays in the body so long.\n\nCould this be a typo? Two likely options:\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a standard starting dose\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose\n\nPlease tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really did mean 50 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical reason so I can add it to the order note. Even then, I'd recommend checking with pharmacy before it's dispensed."
      }
