     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I understand you've confirmed it, but I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation.\n\n**Why:** No adult indication I know of supports 50 mg/day, and the usual maximum is 10 mg/day. At this dose the risk of severe, long-lasting low blood pressure is high, and in a 70 kg adult it could be fatal. Amlodipine overdose is often resistant to treatment and can last more than 24 hours because the drug clears slowly. If this is a typo or a mix-up with another drug or patient, entering it as written could cause serious harm.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- Enter **amlodipine 5 mg** or **10 mg PO once daily**.\n- Enter a different drug, if this was meant for another antihypertensive (for example, losartan 50 mg or metoprolol 50 mg are common 50 mg doses).\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for this dose, please talk to the clinical pharmacist on the medicine service. They can review it and process the order through the usual override process with your reasoning documented.\n\nLet me know which dose or drug you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
